; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-user-identifier-one)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This is a grouped AVP containing either an External Identifier, an MSISDN or an IMSI (exactly one, and only one, of those identifiers shall be included in the request)."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name or User-Identifier/MSISDN or User-Identifier/External-Identifier
    excludes User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/MSISDN or User-Identifier/User-Name and User-Identifier/External-Identifier or User-Identifier/MSISDN and User-Identifier/External-Identifier


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-service-id-s6n)
; AVP: Service-ID
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-scs-identity)
; AVP: SCS-Identity
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the Service-ID indicates DEVICE_TRIGGER (0) or SMS_MO (1), the SCS-Identity shall be formatted as an E.164 address as described in clause 6.4.4."
"In this release, only the Device Triggering and SMS_MO services are supported."
    encoding e164-tbcd
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-service-parameters-s6n)
; AVP: Service-Parameters
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/1
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6n (i.e., when the procedure is invoked by the MTC-AAA), this IE is not applicable, and shall be absent."
    absent-if not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-experimental-result-vendor)
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for S6m/S6n errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-user-identifier-success)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present only when the Result- Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-service-data)
; AVP: Service-Data
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.1
; Table: 5.2.1.1/2
; Page: 14
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present only when the Requested Service IE was included in the request, and the Result- Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    requires request/Service-ID and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-user-identifier-returned)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1.2
; Page: 16
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"if available, the MSISDN of the user shall also be returned by the HSS, along with the user's IMSI."
    text-only
"If it is known, the HSS shall answer successfully and return in the response one or several instances of the User Identity IE, each one containing either an External-Identifier or an MSISDN (if any of these identities are present in the subscriber profile in HSS), or the subscriber's IMSI (if the subscriber does not have any External Identifiers or MSISDNs assigned)."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS and not request/SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-flags-mtc-iwf)
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.3
; Page: 17
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the MTC-IWF sends a Subscriber Information Retrieval request to the HSS, it shall set the S6m/S6n indicator bit in the SIR Flags IE."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-flags-mtc-aaa)
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.4
; Page: 17
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the MTC-AAA sends a Subscriber Information Retrieval request to the HSS, it shall clear the S6m/S6n indicator bit in the SIR Flags IE."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-user-identifier-mtc-aaa)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1.4
; Page: 17
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The MTC-AAA shall only include the User Identifier IE in the request, and it shall contain only the IMSI of the UE."
    requires SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" or User-Identifier/User-Name
    excludes not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/MSISDN or not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/External-Identifier or not SIR-Flags bit "S6m/S6n Indicator" and User-Identifier/LMSI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-no-authorization-lifetime)
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-no-session-timeout)
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-auth-session-state)
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [23]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-no-authorization-lifetime)
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-no-session-timeout)
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Page: 18
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.9
; Page: 19
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    requires Supported-Features/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.9
; Page: 19
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    requires Supported-Features/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-no-vendor-specific-application-id)
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Request
; Section: 6.2.2
; Page: 20
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP shall not be included in any command sent by Diameter nodes supporting applications defined in this specification."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-no-vendor-specific-application-id)
; AVP: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.2.2
; Page: 20
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP shall not be included in any command sent by Diameter nodes supporting applications defined in this specification."
    absent


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Experimental-Result-Code
; Kind: result-codes
; Section: 6.3
; Page: 21
DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN                   = 5001 ; 6.3.3.1 from TS29.229
DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_REQUESTING_ENTITY = 5510 ; 6.3.3.2
DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_SERVICE           = 5511 ; 6.3.3.3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sia-result-code-absent-with-experimental-result)
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Subscriber-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.3.3
; Page: 21
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When one of the result codes defined here is included in a response, it shall be inside an Experimental-Result AVP and the Result-Code AVP shall be absent."
    absent-if Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code in DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN,
        DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_REQUESTING_ENTITY,
        DIAMETER_ERROR_UNAUTHORIZED_SERVICE


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: User-Identifier
; Section: 6.4.2
; Page: 23
User-Identifier ::= < AVP header: 3102 10415 >
        [ User-Name ]
        [ MSISDN ]
        [ External-Identifier ]
        [ LMSI ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#user-identifier-not-empty)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Section: 6.4.2
; Page: 23
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This AVP shall contain at least one of the identifiers used by the UE, i.e., it shall not be empty."
    members at-least-one User-Name MSISDN External-Identifier LMSI


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: Service-ID
; Section: 6.4.3
; Page: 23
Service-ID ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 3103 10415 >
        DEVICE_TRIGGER = 0
        SMS_MO         = 1


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Service-Parameters
; Section: 6.4.5
; Page: 24
Service-Parameters ::= < AVP header: 3105 10415 >
        [ T4-Parameters ]
        [ Application-Port-Identifier ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: T4-Parameters
; Section: 6.4.6
; Page: 24
T4-Parameters ::= < AVP header: 3106 10415 >
        [ Priority-Indication ]
        [ SM-RP-SMEA ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Service-Data
; Section: 6.4.7
; Page: 24
Service-Data ::= < AVP header: 3107 10415 >
        [ T4-Data ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: T4-Data
; Section: 6.4.8
; Page: 24
T4-Data ::= < AVP header: 3108 10415 >
        [ HSS-Cause ]
        [ Serving-Node ]
      * [ Additional-Serving-Node ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#t4-data-serving-node-absent-subscriber)
; AVP: Serving-Node
; Within: T4-Data
; Section: 6.4.8
; Page: 24
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS-Cause indicates Absent Subscriber, via the corresponding flag in the bit mask, the Serving-Node and Additional-Serving-Node AVPs shall not be present."
    absent-if HSS-Cause bit "Absent Subscriber"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#t4-data-additional-serving-node)
; AVP: Additional-Serving-Node
; Within: T4-Data
; Section: 6.4.8
; Page: 24
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS-Cause indicates Absent Subscriber, via the corresponding flag in the bit mask, the Serving-Node and Additional-Serving-Node AVPs shall not be present."
    absent-if HSS-Cause bit "Absent Subscriber"
"Additional-Serving-Node AVP shall be absent if Serving-Node AVP is absent."
    requires Serving-Node


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: HSS-Cause
; Kind: bits
; Section: 6.4.9
; Table: 6.4.9/1
; Page: 25
"Absent Subscriber"           = 0
"Teleservice Not Provisioned" = 1
"Call Barred"                 = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#hss-cause-undefined-bits)
; AVP: HSS-Cause
; Section: 6.4.9
; Table: 6.4.9/1
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"NOTE 2: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the HSS and discarded by the receiving node, MTC-IWF."
    bits only 0 1 2


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Kind: bits
; Section: 6.4.10
; Table: 6.4.10/1
; Page: 25
"S6m/S6n Indicator" = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#sir-flags-undefined-bits)
; AVP: SIR-Flags
; Section: 6.4.10
; Table: 6.4.10/1
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Note: Bits not defined in this table shall be cleared by the sending node, MTC-IWF or MTC-AAA, and discarded by the receiving HSS."
    bits only 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#external-identifier-format)
; AVP: External-Identifier
; Section: 6.4.11
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"For S6m/S6n interface it shall contain an external identifier of the UE. See 3GPP TS 23.003 [11] for the definition and formatting of the External Identifier. For S6t interface, it shall contain an external identifier for an individual UE or a group of UEs, as indicated by Type-Of-External-Identifier AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
Serving-Node ::= < AVP header: 2401 10415 >
        [ SGSN-Name ]
        [ SGSN-Realm ]
        [ SGSN-Number ]
        [ MME-Name ]
        [ MME-Realm ]
        [ MME-Number-for-MT-SMS ]
        [ MSC-Number ]
        [ IP-SM-GW-Number ]
        [ IP-SM-GW-Name ]
        [ IP-SM-GW-Realm ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-number)
; AVP: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"d) MSC-Number"
"f) IP-SM-GW-Number"
    members at-least-one SGSN-Number MME-Number-for-MT-SMS MSC-Number IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-sgsn-number)
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    excludes MME-Name or MME-Realm or MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MSC-Number or IP-SM-GW-Number or IP-SM-GW-Name or IP-SM-GW-Realm


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-sgsn-name)
; AVP: SGSN-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Realm and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-sgsn-realm)
; AVP: SGSN-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Name and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-mme-name)
; AVP: MME-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Realm and MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MME-Realm and MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-mme-realm)
; AVP: MME-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Name


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-mme-number)
; AVP: MME-Number-for-MT-SMS
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
    requires MME-Name and MME-Realm
    excludes MSC-Number or IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-msc-number)
; AVP: MSC-Number
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"d) MSC-Number"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    excludes IP-SM-GW-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-ip-sm-gw-name)
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Name
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"g) IP-SM-GW-Number & IP-SM-GW-Name & IP-SM-GW-Realm"
    requires IP-SM-GW-Number and IP-SM-GW-Realm


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#serving-node-ip-sm-gw-realm)
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Realm
; Within: Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.12
; Page: 25
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"g) IP-SM-GW-Number & IP-SM-GW-Name & IP-SM-GW-Realm"
    requires IP-SM-GW-Number and IP-SM-GW-Name


; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
Additional-Serving-Node ::= < AVP header: 2406 10415 >
        [ SGSN-Name ]
        [ SGSN-Realm ]
        [ SGSN-Number ]
        [ MME-Name ]
        [ MME-Realm ]
        [ MME-Number-for-MT-SMS ]
        [ MSC-Number ]
      * [ AVP ]


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-number)
; AVP: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"d) MSC-Number"
    members at-least-one SGSN-Number MME-Number-for-MT-SMS MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-sgsn-number)
; AVP: SGSN-Number
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"a) SGSN-Number"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    excludes MME-Name or MME-Realm or MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-sgsn-name)
; AVP: SGSN-Name
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Realm and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-sgsn-realm)
; AVP: SGSN-Realm
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"b) SGSN-Name & SGSN-Realm & SGSN-Number if the HSS supports the \"Gdd in SGSN\" feature and has received the \"Gdd in SGSN\" indication over S6a or Gr interface from the SGSN (cf. 3GPP TS 29.272 [4] and 3GPP TS 29.002 [9])"
    requires SGSN-Name and SGSN-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-mme-name)
; AVP: MME-Name
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Realm and MME-Number-for-MT-SMS or MME-Realm and MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-mme-realm)
; AVP: MME-Realm
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
"e) MSC-Number & MME-Name & MME-Realm"
    requires MME-Name


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#additional-serving-node-mme-number)
; AVP: MME-Number-for-MT-SMS
; Within: Additional-Serving-Node
; Section: 6.4.13
; Page: 26
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The following combinations are allowed:"
"c) MME-Name & MME-Realm & MME-Number-for-MT-SMS"
    requires MME-Name and MME-Realm
    excludes MSC-Number


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#ip-sm-gw-number-e164)
; AVP: IP-SM-GW-Number
; Section: 6.4.14
; Page: 27
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"The IP-SM-GW-Number AVP is of type OctetString and it shall contain the ISDN number of the IP-SM-GW in international number format as described in ITU-T Rec E.164 [41]. It shall be encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP shall not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan."
    encoding e164-tbcd


