"IMSI Group Id (See 3GPP TS 29.272 [14])"                 IMSI-Group-Id                              C


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-user-identifier-one)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This is a grouped AVP containing either an External Identifier or an MSISDN (exactly one, and only one, of those identifiers shall be included in the request)."
    requires User-Identifier/External-Identifier or User-Identifier/MSISDN
    excludes User-Identifier/External-Identifier and User-Identifier/MSISDN


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-group-reporting-guard-timer)
; AVP: Group-Reporting-Guard-Timer
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Shall be present if the User-Identifier contains an External Group Identifier."
    present-if User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-additional-identifiers)
; AVP: AdditionalIdentifiers
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-1
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the request is used to retrieve multiple IMSI Group IDs for multiple External Group Identifiers, this information element shall be present and shall contain all the External Group Identifiers for which the IMSI Group IDs are requested, except the one conveyed in the User-Identifier AVP."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-experimental-result-vendor)
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall only be used for S6t errors which are applicable regardless of the services requested (e.g. DIAMETER_ERROR_USER_UNKNOWN). This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-user-identifier)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall not be present if the External-Identifier of User-Identifier in CIR message contains the identity of a Group of UEs (i.e. External Group Identifier). This IE shall be present only when the Result-Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    absent-if request/User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE
    requires Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-number-of-ues)
; AVP: Number-Of-UEs
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present if the External-Identifier of User-Identifier in CIR message contains the identity of a Group of UEs (i.e. External Group Identifier)."
    present-if request/User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-monitoring-event-report)
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If an immediate report is available this information element shall contain the requested data available in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-monitoring-event-config-status)
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Config-Status
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This IE shall be present if Monitoring Event Configuration IE is included in CIR and if the Result-Code AVP in Configuration Information Answer is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if request/Monitoring-Event-Configuration and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-s6t-hss-cause)
; AVP: S6t-HSS-Cause
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"It shall be present if the user is not registered in any serving node."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-enhanced-coverage-restriction-data)
; AVP: Enhanced-Coverage-Restriction-Data
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"It shall be present if the request contained a CIR-Flag AVP with the bit for Enhanced-Coverage-Query set."
    present-if request/CIR-Flags bit "Enhanced Coverage Query" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-imsi-group-id)
; AVP: IMSI-Group-Id
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.1
; Table: 7.2.1.1-2
; Page: 28
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This information element shall be present if the CIR-Flag for IMSI Group Retrieval was set in the request and the Result-Code is DIAMETER_SUCCESS."
    present-if request/CIR-Flags bit "IMSI Group Id retrieval" and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-delete-all-monitoring-events)
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"IF the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all monitoring events, the HSS shall delete all Monitoring events configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes forwarding the deletion to involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new monitoring events."
    absent-if CIR-Flags bit "Delete all Monitoring events" and Monitoring-Event-Configuration/SCEF-Reference-ID or CIR-Flags bit "Delete all Monitoring events" and Monitoring-Event-Configuration/SCEF-Reference-ID-Ext


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-delete-all-communication-pattern)
; AVP: AESE-Communication-Pattern
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all communication pattern, and the feature Config-Eff-CP is supported, the HSS shall delete all Communication Pattern configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes forwarding the deletion to involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new communication pattern."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-delete-all-network-parameter-configurations)
; AVP: Suggested-Network-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the CIR message contains the CIR-Flags with delete all network parameter configurations, and the feature Config-Eff-NP is supported, the HSS shall delete all Suggested Network Configurations configured by the SCEF for the subscriber. This includes the updating of involved serving nodes. In this case the CIR message shall not contain new network parameter configurations."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cia-suggested-network-configuration-unmodified)
; AVP: Suggested-Network-Configuration
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.1.2
; Page: 31
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"When the HSS did not modify parameters received in the Suggested-Network-Configuration AVP, the HSS shall return a Suggested-Network-Configuration AVP to the SCEF in CIA containing only SCEF Reference ID and SCEF-ID."
    text-only


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Page: 35
; Columns: Name                                 AVP                       Cat
"User Identity (see 8.4.36)"                    User-Identifier           C
"Supported Features (See 3GPP TS 29.229 [7])"   Supported-Features        O
"Monitoring Event Report (see 8.4.3)"           Monitoring-Event-Report   O
"Group Report (see 8.4.61)"                     Group-Report              C
"RIR-Flags (see 8.4.63)"                        RIR-Flags                 O
"Supported Services (see 8.4.40)"               Supported-Services        C


; Type: Information Elements
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-2
; Page: 35
; Columns: Name                                 AVP                               Cat
"Result (See 6.3)"                              Result-Code/Experimental-Result   M
"Supported Features (See 3GPP TS 29.229 [7])"   Supported-Features                O
"Monitoring Event Report Status"                Monitoring-Event-Report-Status    O


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-user-identifier)
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Page: 35
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"This AVP shall not carry the IMSI towards the SCEF."
    excludes User-Identifier/User-Name
"For group based configuration processing, the External-Identifier shall be present and contain an External Group Identifier (see 3GPP TS 23.003 [11])."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-monitoring-event-report)
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Page: 35
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If a report is available in the HSS this information element shall contain the requested data available in the HSS."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-group-report)
; AVP: Group-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Page: 35
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Shall be present if User-Identifier contains an External Group Identifier"
    present-if User-Identifier/Type-Of-External-Identifier = EXTERNAL-GROUP-IDENTIFIER-TYPE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-supported-services)
; AVP: Supported-Services
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-1
; Page: 35
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If RIR-flags indicates a change of SCEF authorization for one or more monitoring events, this information element shall be present."
    present-if RIR-Flags bit Change-Of-Authorized-Monitoring-Events


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#ria-experimental-result-vendor)
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 7.2.2.1
; Table: 7.2.2.1-2
; Page: 35
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for S6t errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-group-configuration-in-progress)
; AVP: RIR-Flags
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Page: 37
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the HSS knows that it has additional RIR commands to send for the same group, the HSS shall include the RIR-Flags AVP with the Group-Configuration-In-Progress bit set and restart the Group Guard Timer to the value it originally received in the CIR."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#rir-report-eff-monte)
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Page: 37
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the HSS and SCEF support the Report-Eff-MONTE feature, the HSS shall make use of RIR-flags AVP for a given User-Identity and no Monitoring-Event-Report AVP(s) shall be included."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#group-report-item-partially-cancel)
; AVP: S6t-HSS-Cause
; Within: Group-Report-Item
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Page: 37
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the RIR command is triggered by partially cancelling of group-based monitoring, the S6t-HSS-Cause IE shall be set to \"Group Event Monitoring Partially Cancel\"."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#supported-services-node-type)
; AVP: Node-Type
; Within: Supported-Services
; Section: 7.2.2.2
; Page: 37
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"If the services supported and authorized by the HSS are the same than those supported by the serving node(s), the Node-Type AVP shall be absent."
    text-only


