; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#nir-hss-destination-host)
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: NIDD-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.6
; Page: 42
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"As the HSS knows the address/name and the associated home network domain name of the SCEF to which it sends RIR and NIR commands from a previously received CIR command, both the Destination-Realm and Destination-Host AVPs shall be present in request commands sent by the HSS to the SCEF."
    present-if NIDD-Authorization-Update


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.336.dadx#cir-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Configuration-Information-Request
; Section: 8.1.9
; Page: 43
; Versions: 18.2.0..19.1.0
"On the all reference points as specified in this specification, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    requires Supported-Features/Vendor-Id = 10415


